  "slug": "visualization-gfaidx-7f7d",
  "summary": "Deep-learning structure predictors for RNA, proteins and complexes now need dedicated metrics, comparison tools and experimental fitting checks.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the assessment of AlphaFold-style and related structure predictions rather than their generation. The perspective on biomolecular structure prediction reports that explicit potassium ion addition shifts AF3 predictions, pointing to persistent limitations for proteins, RNA and complexes. For RNA, RNAcomp2D runs multiple secondary structure predictors, including thermodynamic and deep learning methods, and visually compares their outputs, while GSP introduces Geometric Spherical Precision, a multi-scale normalized score for 3D RNA and RNP complex predictions against reference structures. ATSASfold takes a complementary route for monomeric proteins, fitting AlphaFold models to SAXS curves and using a classifier to suggest ATSAS-based refinement strategies. What is new is the combination of multi-method visual comparison, normalized multi-scale scoring and experimental data fitting into workflows for judging predicted models.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
